# Expansion panels

**Never use elevated expansion panels.** Nested in StandardCard they look wrong against the flat card chrome.

```vue
<v-expansion-panels
  v-model="opened"
  multiple
  flat
  variant="accordion"
>
```

## Required

- `flat` — always
- Prefer `variant="accordion"` for flush stacked rows
- `multiple` when more than one panel may be open; start collapsed (`v-model` `[]`); do not set `mandatory`
- After **creating** a list item (new screen, new tour entry), expand that panel, scroll it into view, and apply the theme class `panel-flash` briefly — do not leave the user hunting for what they just added

## Body padding and wash

Theme (`.v-expansion-panel-text__wrapper`) sets **16px** top (Vuetify default is only 8px). With `.v-field` inside, top is **20px** for outlined label clearance. `.v-expansion-panel-text` uses a subtle `on-surface` tint (≈1.5–2.5% opacity) as an inset wash — do not invent per-panel background colors.

## Do not

- Omit `flat` (default elevation/shadow)
- Stack elevated panels as a substitute for StandardCard
- Patch panel top spacing only in one component while leaving others tight
